{{also|Machete}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Machette_kos.pg.jpg|thumb|right|250px|a machete]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|es|machete}}, diminutive of {{m|es|macho||sledgehammer}}, from {{der|en|la|mattea}}, possibly from {{m|la|mactare||slaughter in sacrifice}}; cognate with {{cog|fro|machier}}, {{cog|fr|massue}}, English {{m|fr|mace}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/məˈʃɛ.ti/|/məˈt͡ʃɛ.ti/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-ncalif-machete.ogg|a=Northern California}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-machete.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sword]]-like [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting large [[plant]]s with a [[chop]]ping motion, or used as a [[weapon]].
#: {{hyper|en|knife<qq:sometimes construed as coordinate>}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|q=all sometimes or regionally synonymous|bolo|golok|panga|parang|sundang}}
# A small [[stringed instrument]] from [[Madeira]], [[Portugal]], having a double bulged body, traditionally of wood, with a small rib and four metallic strings, sometimes attached by wooden pegs.

